[aperanton] arm 20 (STAGE Α8b, THE X-TRANSFER MODEL AND THE INFINITE SLAB): XTransfer.lean -- THE CHAIN (the slab's Gibbs sum over all sequences of cross-section configurations is the matrix sandwich of the site weights and the kernel), THE GRAM FACTORISATION of a positive semidefinite matrix and its converse, THE TENSOR KERNEL positive semidefinite and positive with its single-link kernel, the transfer matrix D^1/2 K D^1/2 positive semidefinite and entrywise positive, THE PERRON LIMIT M^a v / lambda_0^a -> <Omega, v> Omega, THE INFINITE SLAB (the centred two-point function of any observable converges to <F Omega, M^R F Omega> / lambda_0^R) and THE STRING TENSION OF THE SLAB MODEL for every finite group; the Z2 link kernel 1 + y s s' positive semidefinite at 0 <= y and positive below 1
[aperanton] arm 21 (STAGE Α8c, THE STRING TENSION IS A GAP): GapBound.lean -- the moment sequence with its Perron mass named (<Omega, f>^2), an observable odd under a permutation fixing M has Perron mass zero (the permutation fixes the Perron line), so the string tension is log lambda_0 - log lambda_k for a NON-Perron eigenvalue: STRICTLY POSITIVE, bounded below by the finite-volume mass gap of its sector; the tensor kernel multiplicative and unital, a left-invertible link kernel making the transfer matrix injective, the quadratic form positive on every nonzero vector; THE Z2 INSTANCE WITH NO HYPOTHESIS LEFT (string_tension_z2: the link kernel's inverse (y + s s')/4y, the gauge flip at one endpoint of the T-line)
[aperanton] arm 23 (STAGE Α8d, THE NONABELIAN WILSON LOOP'S STATIC POTENTIAL): Nonabelian.lean -- an observable whose average over a finite family of M-fixing permutations vanishes has zero Perron mass; every Gram vector of a nontrivial real class function's class matrix sums to zero, so the T-line vectors F_j = phi_j o h average to zero under the endpoint's gauge group; a finite sum of such two-point functions has a static potential E = lim -log W(R)/R that is a gap (log lambda_0 - log lambda_k, lambda_k non-Perron, strictly positive; the static potential of the T-line sector at every separation, in every phase -- the area law not claimed); the loop's pair weight chi(h(c_a) h(c_a+R)^-1) on the slab is the sum over j of F_j's two-insertion sums, each converging to <F_j Omega, M^R F_j Omega> / lambda_0^R for ANY unit Perron vector (the sign immaterial): the nonabelian Wilson loop of the x-transfer model converges and its static potential is at least the gap once W(1) > 0
[aperanton] arm 24 (STAGE Α8e, THE GAUGE ACTION): GaugeAction.lean -- the gauge transformation by g at a vertex (g left of every link out of it, g^-1 right of every link into it) is a permutation of the configurations; a square plaquette's holonomy is conjugated by g at its base corner and unchanged otherwise, so a product of class-function plaquette weights is gauge invariant; the link kernel w(a b^-1) of a class function is invariant under simultaneous left and under right multiplication, so the tensor kernel is gauge invariant; a line leaving the vertex by its first link and never returning has holonomy equivariant, h(gauge c) = g h(c): THE LATTICE THEOREM -- on any finite cross-section of square plaquettes, for any finite group, positive class-function plaquette weight, class-function link weight with positive semidefinite positive kernel, nontrivial real class function with positive semidefinite class matrix, and T-line leaving a vertex once, the nonabelian Wilson loop of the x-transfer model converges and its static potential is at least the sector's gap once W(1) > 0
[aperanton] arm 25 (STAGE Α8f, THE LINEAR ACTION): LinearAction.lean -- for a real orthogonal representation (multiplicative, unital, orthogonal) the inverse is represented by the transpose, so the character's class matrix chi(a b^-1) = tr(rho(a) rho(b)^T) is THE GRAM MATRIX of the representation matrices, positive semidefinite; the average sum_g rho(g) sends every vector to an invariant one, so with no nonzero invariant vector it vanishes and the class matrix kills the constants; |chi(g)| <= d; THE LINEAR ACTION w = C + chi with C > d is a positive class function whose link kernel C J + X is positive semidefinite and positive; THE LATTICE THEOREM FOR THE LINEAR ACTION: three real orthogonal representations (the in-plane weight, the x-plaquette weight, the loop's with no invariant vector), any cross-section of square plaquettes, any T-line leaving a vertex once -- the nonabelian Wilson loop converges and its static potential is at least the sector's gap once W(1) > 0, every representation-theoretic hypothesis discharged
[aperanton] arm 26 (STAGE Α8g, THE SCHUR PRODUCT): Schur.lean -- the entrywise product of two positive semidefinite matrices is positive semidefinite (the Gram matrix of the entrywise products of the two Gram families), so are nonnegative multiples and entrywise powers; the link kernel of a product of class functions is the entrywise product of the kernels, of a sum the sum; hence EVERY POLYNOMIAL IN THE CHARACTER WITH NONNEGATIVE COEFFICIENTS -- the partial sums of the Wilson action among them -- has a positive semidefinite link kernel, and is a positive class function when its constant term dominates
[aperanton] arm 27 (STAGE Α8h, THE WILSON ACTION): Wilson.lean -- the cone of positive semidefinite matrices is closed under entrywise limits (every quadratic form a limit of nonnegative ones); the Wilson action exp(beta chi) is a positive class function whose kernel is the entrywise limit of the polynomial actions' kernels (the partial sums of the exponential series, each positive semidefinite by the Schur product), hence POSITIVE SEMIDEFINITE for beta >= 0: Bochner's condition for the Wilson action of any real orthogonal representation of any finite group, with no Fourier theory; its invertibility (W(1) > 0) not built; THE LATTICE THEOREM FOR THE WILSON ACTION stated as a theorem (wilson_lattice_potential_gap), the composition of every discharged hypothesis, W(1) > 0 alone remaining
